  {
   "id": "bekhorot.40a.22",
   "daf": "40a",
   "sentenceId": 21,
   "he": "וְשֶׁנִּיטַּל רוֹב הַמְדַבֵּר שֶׁבִּלְשׁוֹנוֹ. מַתְנִיתִין מַנִּי? רַבִּי יְהוּדָה הִיא, דְּתַנְיָא: וְאֶת שֶׁנִּיטַּל רוֹב הַלָּשׁוֹן, רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: רוֹב הַמְדַבֵּר שֶׁל לְשׁוֹנוֹ.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «Or that most of» the segment of «its tongue» corresponding to the segment that facilitates «speech» in the tongue of a person «was removed.» The Gemara asks: «Whose» opinion is expressed in «the mishna? It is» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda, as it is taught» in a baraita: «Or that most of its tongue was removed; Rabbi Yehuda says: Most of» the segment of «its tongue» corresponding to the segment that facilitates «speech» in the tongue of a person must be removed to be considered a blemish."
  }
 ],
